+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+On the adversarial synthetic corpus whose vocabulary contained only 30 words,
+the measured full-recall p95 for the `UserPromptSubmit` hook was **10.27 ms**.
+
+The term-selection fix drops a candidate term before IDF ranking when its
+document frequency is greater than one third of the store (`df > n / 3`, for
+stores with at least 50 records). Such terms carry little discriminating signal
+while forcing long posting-list reads. The benchmark corpus was also changed
+from the adversarial 30-word vocabulary to a Zipf-distributed vocabulary (30
+frequent domain words plus 2,000 rare identifiers), so the measured improvement
+should not be attributed to the selector change alone.
+
+After those changes, the measured full-recall p95 for `UserPromptSubmit` was
+**1.82 ms**.
